kind: graph
semantic_diff: >-
  Envelope-changing revision, approved by the user: one outcome, one edge and
  one check added at scope_next_increment; one meaning change at
  execute_attempt_loop; the empty runtime_bindings block. 6 hunks, 38 added lines against 1
  removed. Counts: 32 nodes unchanged, 95 -> 96 edges, 16 -> 17 checks,
  88 -> 89 outcomes.

  (1) PREREQUISITE HOLD AT SCOPING (new outcome prerequisite_unlanded, edge
  prerequisite_to_rescoping, check prerequisite_is_in_plan). The node declared no
  route for "the item the rule would select depends on an unlanded block the plan
  already carries". plan_unrealizable_as_designed re-enters the design boundary
  for what is an ordering fact; increment_selected on the prerequisite hides the
  hold. The lead resolved the field case by ruling on an undeclared route. Now the
  lap holds the item by id, selects the prerequisite, and re-arms the held item at
  the prerequisite's landing; the mechanical check settles that the prerequisite is
  an in-plan unlanded block (otherwise the case is a design change and takes the
  existing door). The precedence list gains it at position 4.

  (2) THE ATTEMPT LOOP REPAIRS ITS OWN TESTS, CONTROLS, LAUNCHERS, CHECKERS AND BUNDLES
  (execute_attempt_loop activity + allowed effect). The node had no write
  allowance in the worktree, so a failing launcher stopped the loop for a lead
  word. Now the diagnosis and fix are recorded together in the attempt log and
  committed; only a product-source change leaves the loop for review. The
  pre-hardware review check impl_commit_is_reviewed is unchanged: a proposal to
  let test- or launcher-only commits keep ready_for_hardware was considered and
  withheld for the user's word.

  (3) runtime_bindings (empty deny and caps). The binding surface the streamlining
  audit's kind: binding proposals fill: deny globs bound to the lead identity and
  per-checkpoint caps, read by the PreToolUse router from this file at the ledger
  head. Empty here; it changes no behaviour until a landed binding fills it.

  FIELD EVIDENCE: (1) the campaign's graph-defect record of 2026-09-10T19:34:05Z
  (a held selection resolved by lead ruling and one plan ordering line); (2) the
  user's ruling of 2026-09-10T17:05:11Z that a lane repairs its own test, control,
  launcher, checker or bundle defects without waiting for the lead, recorded
  verbatim in the campaign log, and the ceremony audit of the same day (two
  workflows, 53 agents) that found the wait lead-invented against a graph that
  neither allowed nor forbade the repair; (3) pave-init 2.6.0 schema. A clause
  saying a CPU-mode acceptance run on an assigned host is no hardware attempt was
  drafted and withheld: no user words cover it and the campaign log counts host
  runs. Reviewed by
  independent adversarial reviewers (fable) as part of the 1.5.5 batch before
  landing.
envelope_check: changed_with_approval
plan_evidence: verified
usage_evidence: field
changelog_entry: >-
  Revision 8 (graph): scope_next_increment gains the prerequisite_unlanded
  outcome, its return edge and the prerequisite_is_in_plan check (an in-plan
  unlanded prerequisite is an ordering hold, not a design change);
  execute_attempt_loop repairs its own tests, controls, launchers, checkers and
  bundles without a lead word; the empty runtime_bindings block is the binding surface for audit
  cuts. 32 nodes, 96 edges, 17 checks, 89 outcomes; 38 added lines against
  1 removed in 6 hunks. Approved by the user 2026-09-10.
